The compressed model scores 16 to 22 points below the uncompressed model on one long document, at every length tried. So far the gap does not get bigger as documents get longer. This is from the first model copy (seed 42) only, so nothing is decided yet.

## Done this wake
- **Three cells finished cleanly:** the seed-42 model on long text, and on mixed documents at 10 and 40 items (mixed = some pages as images, some as their text). Every check passed: all rows scored by the judge, no unreadable verdicts, at most 3.2% of answers hit the 512-token length limit (the bar is 5%), and the number of compressed slots used matched the prediction exactly.
- **Accuracy as judged by the Qwen3-8B grader, higher is better.** Gap = compressed minus uncompressed, same questions, with a 95% confidence interval (CI). Compression is 8 tokens per slot.

| set, size | questions | compressed ↑ | uncompressed ↑ | gap (pt) | gap change vs shortest size (pt) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| pages, 10 | 1,407 | .507 | .672 | −16.6 [−19.5, −13.9] | reference |
| mixed, 10 items | 1,407 | .449 | .654 | −20.5 [−23.3, −17.6] | reference |
| mixed, 40 items | 1,407 | .412 | .631 | −21.9 [−24.7, −18.9] | −1.4 [−4.5, +1.6] |
| text, ~4k tokens | 637 | .422 | .612 | −19.0 | reference |
| text, ~32k tokens | 411 | .377 | .547 | −17.0 | +3.9 [−1.7, +9.7] |

- **Gap change with length:** every CI here includes 0, so there is no sign of a length loss yet. The CIs are still wider than the ±3-point bar the campaign needs to call it "no effect". That call needs both model copies.
- **Four new cells launched**, all running: the second model copy (seed 43) on pages and mixed documents at 10 and 20 items. That uses this wake's limit of four launches.
- **Tool fix:** the script that measures the length effect could not match a question across lengths, because the question ID carries the length as a suffix. I added an option (`--strip_bucket`) to drop the suffix; it is off by default. With the option off, the script still gives exactly the recorded result (+4.3) on an older comparison. With it on, comparing a file against itself gives 0, as it should.
- **Memory:** the 40-page cell is using 12.9 GB while it booked 8 GB, and it keeps running. The cluster does not enforce the booking on these nodes, so this is a booking mistake, not a crash risk. I updated the known-issues table to say so.
- **Updated** `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md`, the state file and the experiment ledger.

## Running now
- **Seed 42:** pages 20 and 40, mixed 20.
- **Seed 43:** text, pages 10 and 20, mixed 10 and 20.

## Next
- **Wake condition:** the next wake starts when the three seed-42 cells end, expected around 03:30–04:00, at most 4 hours from now.
- **On waking:** pair each of those three cells with its uncompressed reference. Then launch seed 43 at 40 pages and 40 mixed items, plus the first two cells comparing long-chunk and short-chunk training on text.
- **Budget:** 77 of 87 cells and about 62 of 114 GPU-hours used. The rest of the plan fits, at about 90 GPU-hours in total.

